In essence, erasure coding transforms the problem from "needing all copies" to "needing enough fragments" — making it the cornerstone of efficient, large-scale redundancy where multiple concurrent failures are expected. For hot data, hybrid approaches (e.g., replication for active data + erasure coding for cold) are common, but pure erasure coding remains the optimal solution for the described scenario.  

